 "metric_source": "sklearn.metrics.average_precision_score (tie-aware) and roc_auc_score",
 "question": "How much of every arm's statement-grain ranking is explained by evidence VOLUME alone -- a bare count off the corpus, with no reading, no model and no belief math?",
 "finding": "Counting distinct source APIs is a strong statement-grain ranker on this panel. Reading clears it, but the headroom above the floor is a small fraction of the raw metric, and no statement-grain claim on this panel is interpretable without it.",
 "why_here": "This panel carries roughly 20 evidence entries per statement and only 20.0% of it is single-evidence, against 62.4%/84.5%/84.3% for eval_curation_v1, external_curator_v1 and holdout_cc. Aggregation does most of the work here and volume is its dominant input, so a statement-grain metric on this panel is partly a measurement of volume.",
 "why_band_1_matters": "The deployed corpus sits at the opposite end. EMMAA averages 2.26 evidences per statement, and 58.16% of all 940,203 statements carry belief exactly 0.65 -- SimpleScorer's value for a single reach evidence, 1-(0.05+0.3) -- with 73.24% on one of two values (research/deployment_plan.md). Band 1 below IS that regime.",
 "single_evidence_shares_for_context": {
  "note": "READ from deployed_baseline_replication.json, never written down here, so this control's framing cannot drift from the artifact that measures it. These are single-EVIDENCE shares, not single-source: results.py tracks those separately (by_n_evidence vs by_n_sources) and they are not interchangeable.",
