  "note": "The same arms scored INSIDE evidence-count bands. Within a band the volume signal is largely held fixed, so what remains is closer to reading quality. Bands are small; these are descriptive, and carry no intervals.",
  "read_distinct_scores_first": "An arm that is constant inside a band scores AUROC 0.5 there by arithmetic, not by judgement. In band 1 the served SimpleScorer emits a single value for every statement, so its 0.5 is the absence of a ranking rather than a bad one -- with one evidence the noisy-OR collapses to that source's prior. This is where the 0.65 modal belief comes from, and band 1 is also the regime the deployment corpus is made of.",
